# UI, Styling, And Accessibility

## Styling

- Use Tailwind CSS 4 through the existing Nuxt/Vite setup and `assets/styles/main.css`.
- Prefer DaisyUI semantic tokens such as `base-*`, `primary`, `secondary`, `accent`, `success`, `warning`, and `error`.
- Avoid raw palette classes for product surfaces when a DaisyUI token communicates the same intent.
- Preserve the current visual language unless the task is explicitly a redesign.

## Components

- Reuse existing cards, buttons, badges, layout helpers, and state-class patterns before adding new variants.
- Keep mobile and desktop behavior intact. Minimum interactive target size is 44px where practical.
- Use `lucide-vue-next` icons consistently; do not add another icon system without approval.

## Accessibility

- Label interactive controls with visible text or `aria-label`.
- Keep focus order logical and visible. Do not remove focus outlines without replacing them.
- Use semantic elements first; add ARIA only when native HTML is not enough.
- Keep contrast at WCAG AA level and avoid color-only state communication.

## Language UI

- Route user-facing copy through i18n when the surrounding feature is localized.
- Mark German learning content with appropriate `lang="de"` when it is rendered inside English UI.
